The driver provides support for the NeoMagic MagicMedia 256AV and
256ZX AC’97 audio devices, found on many laptops.  The MagicMedia
256AV  also comes in a variant (usually found on Dell and HP lap‐
tops) that works in Windows Sound System emulation mode,  not  in
AC’97  mode.  That variant of the chip must be used with the dri‐
ver.  The driver will not attach to such chips.  The device  dri‐
ver appeared in The MagicMedia 256 series is not well‐documented.
No  MIDI or FM synthesizer capability is provided with the Magic‐
Media 256 in AC’97 mode.  While those capabilities  are  provided
by the Windows driver for the chip, they are emulated by the Win‐
dows driver, and not directly supported by the hardware.
